# Workspace UI — Cursor Agent Instructions

You are working on **Workspace UI**, an open-source corporate messenger built on the Zulip API.
The codebase uses **Feature-Sliced Design (FSD)** architecture.

## Quick Facts

- React 19 + TypeScript 5.6 (strict + noUncheckedIndexedAccess) + Vite 6
- Zustand 4.5 stores in `entities/<name>/<name>.model.ts`
- Tailwind CSS 3.4 with 42 semantic design tokens (NO hardcoded colors)
- i18n: English (default) + Russian. ALL UI text via `t("key")`
- Tests: Vitest 4, TDD mandatory for new features. 2100+ tests.
- License: Apache 2.0

## FSD Import Rules (STRICT)

```
app → pages → widgets → features → entities → shared
```

- Import only DOWN the hierarchy. Never up.
- **No barrel `index.ts` re-exports** (see `.cursor/rules/no-barrel-index.mdc`)
- Import from concrete files: `import { X } from "~/entities/user/user.model"`

## Key Paths

| What | Path |
|------|------|
| Entities (stores) | `src/entities/<name>/` |
| Features | `src/features/<name>/` |
| Widgets | `src/widgets/<name>/` |
| Pages | `src/pages/<name>/` |
| App shell | `src/app/` |
| UI primitives | `src/shared/ui/` |
| Utilities | `src/shared/lib/` |
| API client | `src/shared/api/client.ts` |
| Constants | `src/shared/config/constants.ts` |
| Test factories | `src/test/factories.ts` |

## Before Writing Code

1. Read `AGENTS.md` for architecture overview
2. Check relevant `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` for the domain
3. Search existing code — don't duplicate what exists

## Code Quality (non-negotiable)

- `guard.userId()` / `invariant()` at API boundaries
- `React.memo` on every component rendered in `.map()`
- `useCallback` / `useMemo` for props passed to children
- `createLogger("scope")` — NEVER `console.log`
- `sanitizeHtml()` before `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`
- `useEffect` MUST return cleanup for subscriptions/timers
- No `any`. No `@ts-ignore`. No `tabIndex > 0`.

## Verification (run after every change)

```bash
npx tsc --noEmit && npx vitest run
```

## Available Skills (read SKILL.md before complex tasks)

| Skill | When to use |
|-------|------------|
| `full-stack-feature` | New feature implementation |
| `code-review` | Code review or refactoring |
| `bug-investigation` | Bug fix or debugging |
| `design-to-code` | Implementing UI from Figma design |

